From: trzz1214 <162259342+trzz1214@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:07:47 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] HD Rumble dialog: one main switch, controller sidebar,
 apply on Done

- Main HD Rumble switch moves to a bar at the top; one copy only. Off now
  means standard rumble on every controller: Switch pads no longer keep a
  disabled engine that swallowed all rumble, DualSense skips the haptics
  DSP, Xbox stays on plain rumble; all still listed as "HD Rumble off".
- Closing the dialog re-applies the saved settings to connected pads
  (InputCommon::ReapplyRenHDrumSettings, run on the input pump), so no
  replug is needed. Cleanup hands SDL back its normal writes and clears
  SDL's remembered standard rumble before the new mode starts.
- Sidebar shows a connected dot per controller; Overview becomes
  Controllers; recommended row only when settings differ; shorter notes;
  Xbox page drops Step 1/2; footer only after a save.
- Vietnamese translations for the new strings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
